{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564353446,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dc9ffeyoFk5Jf1Ozxoo2","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45ee6790013coFmJGVHTVICa","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dc9ffeyoFk5Jf1Ozxoo2","messageID":"msg_1d45ecceb001yfEFBpfC6m5CLx","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f7e77630d11d68","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '96,112p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md && echo \"---- row ----\" && sed -n '232p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md"},"output":"### Step 3: Durable JSONL Diagnostics\n\nGoal: confirm hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks under the temp metrics root and that `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes.\n\nEvery hook run writes a prompt-free health record to these sinks, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n\n```bash\nexport SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\nls -la \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\nhead -3 \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\n```\n\nThen drive a prompt through any runtime hook (e.g. the Copilot deterministic smoke in Step 5), and confirm a fresh line appears in the sink and is reflected in the next `advisor_validate` telemetry rollup.\n\nPass condition: sinks are bounded (rotation/truncation visible), contain closed-label fields only, and are picked up by `advisor_validate` telemetry rollups.\n\n### Step 4: OpenCode Plugin CLI Smoke\n---- row ----\n| JSONL sink empty or unbounded | Metrics root misconfigured, no prompt hook ran in this checkout or rotation disabled | Check `TMPDIR`, run one prompt through the hook, confirm `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts` sink wiring, and verify rotation bounds |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Step 3: Durable JSONL Diagnostics\n\nGoal: confirm hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks under the temp metrics root and that `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes.\n\nEvery hook run writes a prompt-free health record to these sinks, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n\n```bash\nexport SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\nls -la \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\nhead -3 \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\n```\n\nThen drive a prompt through any runtime hook (e.g. the Copilot deterministic smoke in Step 5), and confirm a fresh line appears in the sink and is reflected in the next `advisor_validate` telemetry rollup.\n\nPass condition: sinks are bounded (rotation/truncation visible), contain closed-label fields only, and are picked up by `advisor_validate` telemetry rollups.\n\n### Step 4: OpenCode Plugin CLI Smoke\n---- row ----\n| JSONL sink empty or unbounded | Metrics root misconfigured, no prompt hook ran in this checkout or rotation disabled | Check `TMPDIR`, run one prompt through the hook, confirm `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts` sink wiring, and verify rotation bounds |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '96,112p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md && echo \\\"---- row ----\\\" && sed -n '232p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564351609,"end":1794564353446}}}}
