{"type":"text","timestamp":1794564385320,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dc9ffeyoFk5Jf1Ozxoo2","part":{"id":"prt_1d45f6936001OXqrcsEDzA8VD3","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44dc9ffeyoFk5Jf1Ozxoo2","messageID":"msg_1d45f55a7001Sq5dtsShfPuJV4","type":"text","text":"T009 is done. Two edits landed in `HV` only, and the task's Verify passes.\n\n**Files written**\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`\n  - Step 3 now reads: \"Every hook run writes a prompt-free health record to these sinks, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\" The code block below it is unchanged.\n  - Troubleshooting row `JSONL sink empty or unbounded`: cause cell is now `Metrics root misconfigured, no prompt hook ran in this checkout or rotation disabled`, and the action cell's `confirm \\`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\\`` became `run one prompt through the hook`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"only occur when\" $HV\n(no output, exit 1)\n\n$ rg -c \"no prompt hook ran in this checkout\" $HV\n1        exit 0\n\n$ rg -c \"export SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\" $HV\n1        exit 0\n```\n\n`git diff` on the file shows exactly the two hunks above. `git status --short -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks` lists my file plus `skill-advisor-hook.md`, which another worker owns (T008) and I did not touch.\n\nNothing could not be done. The checkbox in `tasks.md` is unticked, as instructed, and no git state was changed.\n\nOne thing for the orchestrator: `tasks.md` line 1's description still says the guides should be \"written only with\" debug, which the phase's own T008 to T011 correct — worth checking the spec and plan wording when the coordinator reconciles the packet.","time":{"start":1794564385078,"end":1794564385320}}}
